[Music]  hey everyone welcome to my 2021 work  from home desktop tour where i'm going  to be showing you where i spend most of  my time working studying and making  youtube videos so i was never really  someone who cared about having a clean  desk with multiple monitors and a proper  chair you know mechanical keyboards and  all that i just kind of sat around the  house in random places doing my work but  as we spend more and more time at home  now i realized how important creating a  proper work environment was when it came  to improving productivity and just being  able to focus without too many  distractions  and so over the past five months i've  watched dozens of videos where youtubers  share their desk setups and i got really  inspired by how much thought and effort  was put into them i decided to give it a  go myself and i can say i'm pretty proud  of the end result so let's jump right  into the video and i'll show you around  alright so as we walk into the room the  first thing you'll see is my desk i  bought this desk from amazon and it's  the artist's standing desk and there  were quite a few table tops to choose  from what i really like about this desk  though is that it can adjust to a pretty  decent height  which is really good because i'm pretty  tall but you can save up to five heights  and easily switch between them i would  say this was a pretty good purchase for  me because i don't think i can ever go  back to just using a normal desk again i  kind of need this stand option so i can  see myself using this desk for a long  time now let's move on to what i have on  my desk so to power up my workstation i  use this macbook pro and this was sent  to me by work so i use this for my day  to day tasks editing videos and just  everything work related i also have a  personal laptop that i use for  everything non-work related like  watching movies playing games all that  and if i ever want to switch between the  two i just plug it in the monotop and  i'll be able to use that instead so for  my laptop stand i decided to get this 12  south book arc and you can prop your  laptop in here oops the wrong way around  you can pop it in here and  it can sit quite nicely on the desk i  think it looks quite aesthetic it's  quite sleek a bit overpriced in my  opinion  but i think the only other negative part  to it is that your laptop is clamped  shut so you can't really do video calls  without having an external webcam since  i don't have an external webcam i need  to just open up the laptop while i do my  video course so i won't be able to use  this all the time next i have this  keyboard and mouse  so the keyboard is the keychron k2 at  the start when i was using it i was  getting a lot of wrist pain and my hands  are hurting because it's too high so i  wouldn't recommend this for people who  just want to get this keyboard by itself  what i had to do was i had to buy this  extra wrist rest and i've been having no  pain or any troubles with the keyboard  ever since it's pretty good because it  has a nice sound to it  and i bought the one that sounds the  most quiet so that during my work cause  and everything i'm not going to be  distracting everyone else this mouse was  one of the cheapest wireless mouse i  could find by logitech and i got this  off amazon and i didn't really find the  need to buy one of those fancy  mouse's nice mouse that have a lot more  extra functionalities my favorite item  on the desk by far is this dboom tv max  and this is essentially a bluetooth  speaker but it has so many more  functionalities and one of my favorite  functionalities is the fact that it can  display some pixel art i can connect it  to my phone and select the artwork i  want there's thousands of artworks to  choose from and you can also create your  own so pretty cool i really like it  because i can just choose any image i  want put it down on the side and it's  something nice to have beside me as i do  my day-to-day tasks  so for multiple screens and a bigger  display i decided to go with these two  dell monitors and also a vivo monitor  arm i actually got these two monitors  for free because they came with my  amazon internship but i decided to get a  monitor mount so that i can have these  two monitors side by side and for it to  have more of a floating effect moving on  to the next thing on my desk this is a  t2 water bottle and it specifically is  designed to put tea leaves inside and  you can pour hot water and it's double  insulated by glass i really like it i  think it's quite  portable and it's  it's able to keep  water or tea quite warm next we have  this little plant i think i got it from  kmart like five six years ago  there's nothing  really useful about this i think it just  adds a bit of a nice touch we have these  coasters  there's four of them i probably only  need one at a time to be honest 70 from  amazon probably not really worth the  cost  but i think it looks really nice on the  desk it adds a really nice touch to it  it's very similar to this plant except  this plant was only like three dollars  but yeah really like it and whenever i  have a jug of hot water or anything like  that i can just put it on top of the  coasters and that way it won't be able  to leave any marks on my desk next i  have this wireless rechargeable lamp you  can change the color just by tapping on  it it's rgb  you can also use a remote control to  control the colors even further but i  think i lost the remote but yeah it was  25 and i think it was pretty worth the  price and i recommend getting it linked  in the description below i also have  this wireless charger which i really  like because i can just prop my phone  directly on it and be able to use the  face id without having to take it off or  get distracted something else on my desk  that i really like are these sony  wireless headphones these are noise  cancelling and yeah i can't really hear  myself anymore but i use this when  listening to music and also for watching  videos not only for video course because  i wanted to just use something wired  something simple and also i want to be  able to hear myself during the course  but this is really good for listening to  music and booking out noise when i need  to i also have these printed daily  planner sheets  and i was always trying to find a really  good tracking system to plan out my days  and i've tried all sorts of online  methods you know lotion all of that it  just never really worked for me because  i prefer pen and paper a bit extra but  what i did was i designed this on canva  so i included the day  urgent not urgent for tomorrow and long  term and i also have a daily highlight  so as long as i get whatever is on my  daily highlight done i'll feel like  that's a productive day on my desk  there's also this huge  mouse desk pad that's  double sided so  red and black and this keeps my desk  from getting dirty because i'm  protecting it by using this one more  thing on my desk is this blue yeti  microphone i use this for voiceovers for  my videos but not really for voice calls  or anything like that  so i only use it occasionally not all  the time but this is just something i  put on my desk as well under my desk is  where i hide the whole mess of cables  there are so many different cables that  i need to power up my workstation and i  have these two wire boxes in order for  me to store everything neatly and to add  a bit of an ambient glow to my setup i  have a lifx strip running along the edge  of my desk and i can use my phone to  control the colors and the brightness  and there you have it that was my 2021  work from home desk setup please let me  know in the comments below what your  favorite item is in the whole setup as  always please give this video a like if  you enjoyed it but yeah thank you for  watching and i'll see you next time bye  for now

